        "comments": [
          {
            "is_markdown": true,
            "count": 0,
            "text": "## Summary\n\nNice to have: `unique()`, `duplicated()` and `anyDuplicated()` can take seconds on a few thousand strings when one of them is a long latin1 string. The attached patch makes this fast without changing any results.\n\n## Details\n\nWith a marked encoding present, `sequal()` in `src/main/unique.c` falls back to `Seql()`, which translates both strings to UTF-8 on every hash probe, so a long latin1 string is translated again for each lookup that probes past it. `shash()` also skips each string's first byte, apparently an oversight, so `\"\"`, all one-character strings, and all strings differing only in their first byte hash alike. Found by OSS-Fuzz as a timeout.\n\nReproducible example: attached as `unique-latin1-translate-repro.R`; its two cases take 8.8 s and 1.7 s on r90913 (macOS), well under a second with the patch.\n\nProposed patch: attached as `unique-latin1-translate.diff`; since translating latin1 never shortens it, `sequal()` rejects a latin1 string against a shorter string that needs no translation, and `shash()` hashes from the first byte. Results are unchanged on 2000 random mixed-encoding vectors; a regression test is added to `tests/reg-fuzz.R`.\n\nThe patch is also submitted as https://github.com/r-devel/r-svn/pull/499, where CI results can be seen.",
            "bug_id": 19329,
            "creator": "kevinushey",
            "creation_time": "2026-11-17T02:06:08Z",
            "is_private": false,
            "time": "2026-11-17T02:06:08Z",
